// Genomes for the music's instruments. The patches in patches.ron are
// generated from this file; edit here, then regenerate:
//   cargo run --release -p tarborn_music --bin patches -- [preview-dir]
//
// Per instrument:
//   role                 what it is for, in words
//   pitched true, root 69, filter_tracking 1, gate false, gain 1
//                        copied to the patch (see patches.ron)
//   measure_length 0.25  seconds a gated instrument is held when measured
//   layers               one range set per synth layer (see below)
//   targets              where the rendered root note must measure:
//     attack   seconds from onset to 90% of peak
//     decay    seconds from peak until it stays 30 dB down
//     centroid spectral centroid in Hz (brightness)
//     noisiness share of power outside the strongest tonal_bins bins:
//              0 a few clean partials .. 1 noise
//
// A layer range set holds the tarborn_sfx layer fields as (min, max); a field
// left out keeps the synth default. `waves` lists the waves to pick from.
// freq, lowpass and highpass are ratios of the root pitch; freq_end,
// duty_end, lowpass_end and highpass_end are ratios of their start value.
// Ranges with a positive minimum are sampled evenly in log space.
(
    analysis: (
        frame: 0.001,
        onset_level: 0.05,
        attack_level: 0.9,
        decay_db: -30.0,
        window: 4096,
        tonal_bins: 32,
    ),
    search: (
        seed: 1,
        candidates: 400,
        centre_weight: 0.05,
        time_floor: 0.001,
        sample_rate: 44100,
